• G1 (Complete Food and Dish Delivery) is an overall Achieve goal that is satisfied only if all three main sub-goals are fulfilled:  
  – G1.1 (Food Delivery)  
  – G1.2 (Dish Retrieval)  
  – G1.3 (Door Opening)  
  This is represented as an AND decomposition:  
   G1.Runtime = ((FALLBACK(G1.1.1, G1.1.2)) AND G1.2 AND G1.3)

• G1.1 (Food Delivery) uses an OR (fallback) decomposition:  
  – G1.1.1 (Direct Table Delivery)  
  – G1.1.2 (Tray Retrieval Assistance)  
  Thus, G1.1.Runtime = FALLBACK(G1.1.1, G1.1.2)

• G1.1.2 (Tray Retrieval Assistance) is further decomposed sequentially:  
  – G1.1.2.0 (Query Patient Record)  
  – G1.1.2.1 (Identify Meal for Retrieval)  
  – G1.1.2.2 (Track Meal Retrieval)  
  – G1.1.2.3 (Alert on Wrong Meal)  
  G1.1.2.Runtime = (G1.1.2.0 ; G1.1.2.1 ; G1.1.2.2 ; G1.1.2.3)

• G1.2 (Dish Retrieval) is also an OR decomposition:  
  – G1.2.1 (Unassisted Dish Retrieval)  
  – G1.2.2 (Cooperative Dish Retrieval)  
  G1.2.Runtime = FALLBACK(G1.2.1, G1.2.2)

• G1.2.2 (Cooperative Dish Retrieval) further uses an OR fallback:  
  – G1.2.2.1 (Robot-Robot Cooperation)  
  – G1.2.2.2 (Human-Robot Cooperation)  
  G1.2.2.Runtime = FALLBACK(G1.2.2.1, G1.2.2.2)

• G1.3 (Door Opening) is an OR (fallback) decomposition:  
  – G1.3.1 (Self-Door Opening)  
  – G1.3.2 (Human-Aided Door Opening)  
  G1.3.Runtime = FALLBACK(G1.3.1, G1.3.2)

• Tasks are directly linked to the leaf perform goals. For example:  
  – AT1 (Place Food on Table) is assigned to G1.1.1.  
  – AT2 and AT3 are linked to G1.1.2.2 and G1.1.2.3, respectively.  
  – AT4, AT5, and AT6 are linked to G1.2.1, G1.2.2.1, and G1.2.2.2, respectively.  
  – AT7 and AT8 are linked to G1.3.1 and G1.3.2, respectively.

──────────────────────────────
